<Routines>
<Routine Name="cold_start_service" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The cold start service is called to initialize everything from scratch, reset the paths, startup, and order all vehicles to 
an initial station to get the system going.  At step 5, the cold start service is dormant and doesn't do anything (so we return from the routine)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,5)RET();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At Step 10 call init_constants and init_stations to get everything initialized.
Clear the timeout counts for postition / path commands.
Set the HLC link status initially down and prev heartbeat to current one so hlc_link_monitor can determine initially if we are talking to the HLC upon first hlc_link_monitor_timer expiry.
Run for loop routine to clear the active flag for each entry in the pos_order tag.  Logic will later select which entries in that array to have the HLC pay attention to.
This routine will start the system and discover all vehicles on the track.
Set the path cmd and position order msg service routine steps to 10 so they are available for work.
Then move on to step 20]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,10)[JSR(init_constants,0) JSR(init_stations,0) ,MOV(0,msg_position_order_timeout_count) MOV(0,msg_path_cmd_timeout_count) ,MOV(0,msg_terminus_cmd_timeout_count) MOV(0,msg_dio_cmd_timeout_count) ,OTU(hlc_link_status) MOV(MMI_heartbeat,previous_hlc_heartbeat) RES(hlc_link_monitor_timer) ,MOV(10,msg_service_path_cmd_step) MOV(10,msg_service_move_to_pos_step) ,MOV(0,i) MOV(15,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the active flag for all 8 entries in the position_order MSG source area
Logic outside here chooses which entries the HLC should pay attention to in
the MSG content by setting active_flag for a particular element.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop3)EQU(cold_start_service.step,15)[MOV(0,position_order[i].active_flag) ,LES(i,7) ADD(i,1,i) JMP(loop3) ,MOV(1,v) MOV(16,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear all records in the vehicle manager storage array
This will allow the vehicle manager array to be repopulated only with detected and ordered vehicle
Prevents stale data]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop4)EQU(cold_start_service.step,16)[MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id) MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].arrived_station_id) ,MOV(VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_IDLE,vehicle_mgr_array[v].state) MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].order_number) MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].PID_set) ,MOV(VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_IDLE,vehicle_mgr_array[v].state) LES(v,max_vehicle_id) ADD(v,1,v) JMP(loop4) ,MOV(17,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set up variables for step 18
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,17)MOV(0,nc_operational)MOV(1,t)MOV(18,cold_start_service.step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wait for all NCs to be in the operational state before resetting.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop8)EQU(cold_start_service.step,18)[EQU(3,MMI_node_controller_status[t].state) ADD(nc_operational,1,nc_operational) ,LES(t,max_nc_id) ADD(t,1,t) JMP(loop8) ,EQU(nc_operational,max_nc_id) MOV(20,cold_start_service.step) ,NEQ(nc_operational,max_nc_id) MOV(17,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When at step 20 and HLC link is up and path cmd msg service is available for work, format a reset command in path_cmd tag.
Set path_id to zero for all paths, reset command, active flag so HLC acts on this single path cmd entry.
use next_command_count routine to get a new command count and store in cold_start_service.  Store command count in path_cmd
Set the msg_service_path_cmd_step to 20 to let the msg service do the msg for us.
Set up the cold start service timer for 10 seconds so we can wait for path command completion or timeout so we can retry.
Go to next step 30
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,20)XIC(hlc_link_status)EQU(msg_service_path_cmd_step,10)[JSR(next_command_count,0,cold_start_service.command_count) ,MMI_Format_Path_Command(MFPC_AOI,0,MMI_RESET_CMD,cold_start_service.command_count,path_cmd) MOV(20,msg_service_path_cmd_step) ,MOV(300000,cold_start_service.timer.PRE) RES(cold_start_service.timer) MOV(25,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initialize variables for step 30
restart cold start routine if process times out]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,25)[MOV(0,paths_done_with_cmd) MOV(1,p) MOV(30,cold_start_service.step) ,XIC(cold_start_service.timer.DN) MOV(20,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At step 30, set the number of paths done with our command to 0
Run a loop to check if each path has finished reset by seeing if the last accepted command for all paths has completed.
if it has, the logic increments paths_done_with_cmd to the number of paths that have completed reset.
When all paths have completed reset, it advances to the next step]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop5)EQU(cold_start_service.step,30)[EQU(MMI_path_command_status[p].last_command_accepted_count,cold_start_service.command_count) EQU(MMI_path_command_status[p].last_command_accepted_completion_status,MMI_CMD_COMPLETE) ADD(paths_done_with_cmd,1,paths_done_with_cmd) ,LES(p,max_path_id) ADD(p,1,p) JMP(loop5) ,EQU(paths_done_with_cmd,max_path_id) MOV(50,cold_start_service.step) ,NEQ(paths_done_with_cmd,max_path_id) MOV(25,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset is done, when path_cmd msg service is ready at step 10, format a startup command the same way we formatted the reset command above and tell msg service to kick the command and set a timeout again.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,50)EQU(msg_service_path_cmd_step,10)[JSR(next_command_count,0,cold_start_service.command_count) ,MMI_Format_Path_Command(MFPC_AOI,0,MMI_STARTUP_CMD,cold_start_service.command_count,path_cmd) MOV(20,msg_service_path_cmd_step) ,MOV(5000,cold_start_service.timer.PRE) RES(cold_start_service.timer) MOV(55,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initialize variables for step 60
restart cold start routine if process times out]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,55)[MOV(0,paths_done_with_cmd) MOV(1,p) MOV(60,cold_start_service.step) ,XIC(cold_start_service.timer.DN) MOV(20,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[At step 60, set the number of paths done with our command to 0
Run a loop to check if each path has finished startup by seeing if the last accepted command for all paths has completed.
if it has, the logic increments paths_done_with_cmd to the number of paths that have completed reset.
When all paths have completed startup, it advances to the next step]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop6)EQU(cold_start_service.step,60)[EQU(MMI_path_command_status[p].last_command_accepted_count,cold_start_service.command_count) EQU(MMI_path_command_status[p].last_command_accepted_completion_status,MMI_CMD_COMPLETE) ADD(paths_done_with_cmd,1,paths_done_with_cmd) ,LES(p,max_path_id) ADD(p,1,p) JMP(loop6) ,EQU(paths_done_with_cmd,max_path_id) MOV(70,cold_start_service.step) ,NEQ(paths_done_with_cmd,max_path_id) MOV(55,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When startup is done, set our timer for 1 second to give the HLC a chance to push the latest vehicle status for all located
vehicles into the MMI_vehicle_status array so we can go through there and determine how many vehicles we have located.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,70)MOV(1000,cold_start_service.timer.PRE)RES(cold_start_service.timer)MOV(80,cold_start_service.step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When our 1 second wait after startup is complete at step 80, move on to step 90]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,80)XIC(cold_start_service.timer.DN)MOV(90,cold_start_service.step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initialize variables for step 100]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(cold_start_service.step,90)MOV(1,v)MOV(100,cold_start_service.step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Go through each vehicle record in MMI_vehicle_status and determine valid vehicles we have found (path ID field in MMI_vehicle_status record is non-zero) and
schedule with the vehicle manager to order each discovered vehicle to an initial station to get things going.  Set the step to 5, cold start complete.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loop7)EQU(cold_start_service.step,100)[XIO(CleanoutPallets) NEQ(MMI_vehicle_status[v].Path_ID,0) MOV(33,vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id) ,XIC(CleanoutPallets) NEQ(MMI_vehicle_status[v].Path_ID,0) MOV(34,vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id) ,LES(v,max_vehicle_id) ADD(v,1,v) JMP(loop7) ,MOV(5,cold_start_service.step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Pet the cold start service timer every scan]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[TON(cold_start_service.timer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="hlc_link_monitor" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(3000,hlc_link_monitor_timer.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This routine watches the MMI_Heartbeat tag from the HLC and sets hlc_link_status when it is known the HLC is talking to us (heartbeat is changing)
and clears hlc_link_status when it is known the HLC is not talking to us (no heartbeat change).

Pet the hlc_link_monitor_timer tag every scan]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[TON(hlc_link_monitor_timer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When link monitor timer is done (3 seconds), check if heartbeat changed -- if so and link is considered down, latch it to up.
If heartbeat didn't change and the link is considered up, latch it down.
Copy the current heartbeat to previous for the next check and reset the timer for the next go-around.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(hlc_link_monitor_timer.DN)[NEQ(MMI_heartbeat,previous_hlc_heartbeat) XIO(hlc_link_status) OTL(hlc_link_status) ,EQU(MMI_heartbeat,previous_hlc_heartbeat) XIC(hlc_link_status) OTU(hlc_link_status) ,MOV(MMI_heartbeat,previous_hlc_heartbeat) RES(hlc_link_monitor_timer) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="init_constants" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[init_constants is called first by the cold_start_service to initialize tag values used as constants.

Convenience constants to have human readable variable names for values right out of the MagneMotion PLC Interface Control Document]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,MMI_CMD_ACCEPTED)MOV(0,MMI_CMD_IN_PROGRESS)MOV(128,MMI_CMD_COMPLETE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,MMI_DIRECTION_BIDIRECTIONAL)MOV(1,MMI_DIRECTION_FORWARD)MOV(2,MMI_DIRECTION_BACKWARD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(1,MMI_JOYSTICK_ENABLE_COMMAND)MOV(2,MMI_JOYSTICK_DISABLE_COMMAND);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(1,MMI_NODE_DEVICE_STATUS_INIT)MOV(2,MMI_NODE_DEVICE_STATUS_FAULTED)MOV(3,MMI_NODE_DEVICE_STATUS_OPERATIONAL);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(178,MMI_STARTUP_CMD)MOV(179,MMI_RESUME_CMD)MOV(180,MMI_SUSPEND_CMD)MOV(184,MMI_RESET_CMD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,MMI_PATH_STATE_INIT)MOV(1,MMI_PATH_STATE_STARTUP)MOV(2,MMI_PATH_STATE_OPERATIONAL)MOV(3,MMI_PATH_STATE_RESET)MOV(4,MMI_PATH_STATE_PROGRAMMING);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[

Adjust for your system.  This example is a very simple single path with 2 stations and up to 15 vehicles
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(6,max_path_id)MOV(13,max_motor_id)MOV(35,max_station_id)MOV(30,max_vehicle_id)MOV(1,max_nc_id);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The possible station states]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(1,STATION_STATE_IDLE)MOV(2,STATION_STATE_DWELL)MOV(3,STATION_STATE_PROCESSING)MOV(4,STATION_STATE_DEPART);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Possible vehicle manager states]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(1,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_IDLE)MOV(2,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_PLACE_ORDER)MOV(3,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
