<Routine Name="vehicle_loc" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the active flag for all 8 entries in the position_order MSG source area
Logic outside here chooses which entries the HLC should pay attention to in
the MSG content by setting active_flag for a particular element.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(loc)[EQU(vehicle,0) [CLR(vehicles_in_path[1]) CLR(vehicles_in_path[2]) CLR(vehicles_in_path[3]) ,CLR(vehicles_in_path[4]) CLR(vehicles_in_path[5]) CLR(vehicles_in_path[6]) ] ,MOV(MMI_vehicle_status[vehicle].Path_ID,loc) ADD(vehicles_in_path[loc],1,vehicles_in_path[loc]) ,LES(vehicle,25) ADD(vehicle,1,vehicle) JMP(loc) ,EQU(loc,0) MOV(0,vehicles_in_path[0]) MOV(0,vehicle) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="vehicle_mgr" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The vehicle_mgr routine is called of a FOR loop in the main_routine to go through each vehicle_mgr_array entry and see if it's IDLE and picked up
an order to a station -- if so the order will be scheduled with the msg service.

For vehicles on their way in WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL state, this routine checks if the vehicle's order is complete and sets it to arrived in
the stations_array for the station_mgr to do it's work upon a vehicle arrival.


When this vehicle_mgr_array entry is IDLE and it picked up a dest_station_id (non-zero), and the msg_service is available
to place an order for us, go to the PLACE_ORDER state to format and schdule the order with the msg_service.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(vehicle_mgr_array[v].state,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_IDLE)NEQ(vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id,0)EQU(msg_service_move_to_pos_step,10)MOV(VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_PLACE_ORDER,vehicle_mgr_array[v].state);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When we hit the PLACE_ORDER state, save the arrived_station_id field and zero it out in this vehicle_mgr_array entry -- this vehicle is going to depart!
Save the dest_station_id field in the vehicle_mgr_array record in dest_station_id.
Set first order entry in position_order array to the path the dest_station_id is on.
Set the position in position_order entry to the position along the path we need to go to.

When this vehicle wasn't sitting at a station (arrived_station_id is zero -- which happens upon initial order at cold start), use fixed values to place the initial order.
When the vehicle is sitting at a station, use this station's velocity, accel, direction (which go with the next station vehicle is heading to).

Get a new order number, use a Bit field distribute instruction to move the binary form of the PID value into the correct section og the flags and direction byte, set active_flag in position_order array entry, and schedule the order
with the msg_service and go to the WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL state.  When there are multiple vehicles that need to get ordered,
this routine round-robins through the vehicle list scheduling orders with the msg_service who turns around getting the orders off 
quickly, so multiple vehicles will simply get ordered in rapid succession off the one MSG instruction used in the MSG service.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(vehicle_mgr_array[v].state,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_PLACE_ORDER)[MOV(vehicle_mgr_array[v].arrived_station_id,arrived_station_id) MOV(vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id,dest_station_id) ,MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].arrived_station_id) JSR(next_command_count,0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].order_number) ,EQU(arrived_station_id,0) MMI_Format_Position_Order(MFPO_AOI,v,stations_array[dest_station_id].path_id,stations_array[dest_station_id].position,stations_array[dest_station_id].velocity,stations_array[dest_station_id].acceleration,vehicle_mgr_array[v].order_number,stations_array[dest_station_id].direction,position_order[0]) ,NEQ(arrived_station_id,0) MMI_Format_Position_Order(MFPO_AOI,v,stations_array[dest_station_id].path_id,stations_array[dest_station_id].position,stations_array[arrived_station_id].velocity,stations_array[arrived_station_id].acceleration,vehicle_mgr_array[v].order_number,stations_array[arrived_station_id].direction,position_order[0]) ,BTD(vehicle_mgr_array[v].PID_set,0,position_order[0].direction,4,4) ,MOV(20,msg_service_move_to_pos_step) MOV(VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL,vehicle_mgr_array[v].state) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When in the WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL state, check if the last order accepted for this vehicle is complete,  store the station vehicle is heading to
 in dest_station_id and check the station vehicle is heading to is free (station's active_vehicle_id field is zero), if so the vehicle arrived:
Store the vehicle ID (which is index i) in the station's active_vehicle_id field so the station_mgr will know a vehicle of ID i has arrived at the station it was heading to!
Set the arrived_station_id field of the vehicle_mgr record to the station id for convenience -- this vehicle is now at the station it was heading to.

Set the vehicle_mgr station to IDLE to wait for the station_mgr to set our dest_station_id field to non-zero when it's time for us to head
to another station.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(vehicle_mgr_array[v].state,VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_WAIT_FOR_ARRIVAL)EQU(MMI_vehicle_order_status[v].last_order_number_accepted,vehicle_mgr_array[v].order_number)EQU(MMI_vehicle_order_status[v].last_order_accepted_is_complete,1)[MOV(vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id,dest_station_id) ,EQU(stations_array[dest_station_id].active_vehicle_id,0) [MOV(v,stations_array[dest_station_id].active_vehicle_id) ,MOV(dest_station_id,vehicle_mgr_array[v].arrived_station_id) ,MOV(0,vehicle_mgr_array[v].dest_station_id) ,MOV(VEHICLE_MGR_STATE_IDLE,vehicle_mgr_array[v].state) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
